              "text": "When drafting complex estate documents like **Testamentary Trusts**, **Enduring Powers of Attorney (EPOA)**, and **comprehensive Wills**, it is advisable to use practitioners with specific expertise in Queensland succession law, tax considerations, and asset protection.\n\nSeveral top-rated and established law firms serve the **Indooroopilly** and **Centenary Suburbs** (Jindalee, Mount Ommaney, Middle Park, Sinnamon Park, and Oxley):\n\n---\n\n### 1. Centenary Suburbs (Jindalee, Mount Ommaney & Surrounds)\n\n* **Jindalee Lawyers (Jindalee)**\n  * **Location:** Jindalee (serving the wider Centenary area).\n  * **Focus:** A community-focused firm with decades of combined legal experience. \n  * **Estate Services:** Known locally for accessible, transparent pricing and practical advice on estate planning. They routinely draft both standard wills and multi-beneficiary **Testamentary Trust Wills**, as well as Enduring Powers of Attorney.\n  * **Why consider them:** Convenient local office in Jindalee, strong client ratings, and approachable communication without excessive jargon.\n\n* **Harding Richards Lawyers (Oxley / Centenary Border)**\n  * **Location:** Oxley (directly adjacent to Jindalee and Seventeen Mile Rocks).\n  * **Focus:** Comprehensive business, property, and private client legal practice.\n  * **Estate Services:** Highly experienced in advising on asset protection, blended family scenarios, and **Testamentary Discretionary Trusts**. They coordinate closely with financial planners and accountants to align trusts and powers of attorney with superannuation and business entities.\n  * **Why consider them:** Strong track record handling commercial and asset-protection overlays in estate planning.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Indooroopilly & Surrounds (Kenmore / Taringa)\n\n* **Kenmore Lawyers (Kenmore)**\n  * **Location:** Moggill Road, Kenmore (just minutes from Indooroopilly, Chapel Hill, and Fig Tree Pocket).\n  * **Focus:** Private client matters, conveyancing, and succession law.\n  * **Estate Services:** Experienced in drafting everything from single wills to **complex estate structures, including testamentary trusts** and EPOAs. \n  * **Why consider them:** Proximity to Indooroopilly residents with off-street suburban parking, offering tailored personal attention.\n\n* **Clear Legal (Indooroopilly)**\n  * **Location:** Indooroopilly.\n  * **Focus:** Boutique practice offering tailored commercial, property, and estate services.\n  * **Estate Services:** Drafting wills, powers of attorney, and providing initial succession guidance.\n  * **Why consider them:** Located right in Indooroopilly for clients who prefer an in-person firm close to Indooroopilly Shopping Centre/rail connections.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Dedicated Estate Planning Specialists Servicing the Western Corridor\n\nFor particularly complex estates (e.g., large super balances, family discretionary trusts, companies, or blended families), you may want a **QLS Accredited Specialist in Succession Law**:\n\n* **Estate First Lawyers (Toowong / Milton Corridor)**\n  * **About:** Founded by Ann Janssen, a Queensland Law Society Accredited Specialist in Succession Law and registered Trust and Estate Practitioner (STEP).\n  * **Services:** They practise **exclusively** in wills and estate planning. They are widely considered industry leaders in structuring **Testamentary Trusts** for tax efficiency and family asset protection.\n  * **Location:** Just a 5–10 minute drive inbound from Indooroopilly down Coronation Drive / Milton Road (they also offer virtual consultations across the western suburbs).\n\n* **Mobile / In-Home Succession Lawyers (e.g., Kate Redman & Associates / Direct Lawyers)**\n  * **About:** Niche firms that specialise solely in succession law and travel directly to clients’ homes across Indooroopilly, Jindalee, Mount Ommaney, and Kenmore.\n  * **Services:** Comprehensive estate packages (Testamentary Trust Will + EPOA + Advance Health Directive) without requiring an in-office appointment.\n\n---\n\n### What to Look for When Requesting Quotes\n\n1. **Testamentary Trust Experience:** Ensure the lawyer explicitly explains the difference between an outright gift and a *testamentary discretionary trust* (including capital gains tax and streaming advantages for children under 18).\n2. **Custom Clauses in the EPOA:** A properly drafted Queensland EPOA should address \"conflict transactions\" (e.g., if your attorney needs to deal with joint bank accounts, family trust control, or real estate), which generic templates often overlook.\n3. **Superannuation & Non-Estate Assets:** Confirm that the quoted service includes advice on **Binding Death Benefit Nominations (BDBNs)**, as superannuation does not automatically pass under a Will.\n4. **Fee Transparency:** Most western suburbs solicitors offer **fixed-fee estate planning packages** for a Will (incorporating testamentary trusts) and an Enduring Power of Attorney. Ask for a fixed quote upfront.",
